The proxy initialises once, and only with an open session; the service touches it before closing:

```java
String getName() {
    if (!initialized) {
        if (!session.open) throw new LazyInitializationException("could not initialize proxy [Customer#" + id + "] - no Session");
        String loaded = session.selectCustomerName(id);
        if (loaded == null) throw new EntityNotFoundException("Unable to find Customer with id " + id);
        name = loaded;
        initialized = true;
    }
    return name;
}

static OrderView view(Supplier<Session> sessions, long orderId, long customerId) {
    try (Session s = sessions.get()) {
        Order order = loadOrder(s, orderId, customerId);
        return new OrderView(order.id(), order.customer().getName());
    }
}
```

The tests catch the plausible wrong version that queries on every call without checking the session (the open-in-view habit): after close it fails with the session's own `IllegalStateException` instead of `LazyInitializationException`, and the boundary test shows that an initialised proxy must not query again. A `view` that returns the entity, or forgets try-with-resources, leaves the session open after a failed load.
